      "content": "Gnomes? \n\nI'm honestly a bit confused. I'm trying to solve a high-stakes professional problem in my kitchen, and you've gone from talking about thermodynamic equilibrium to \"fat-loving gnomes\" building mounds. \n\nAre you saying there's some kind of actual, widely-recognized way in confectionery science to personify these micro-fluctuations, or is this just a metaphor you're using? Because if I'm going to troubleshoot my cooling racks and surface stability, I need to know if there's a technical basis for this \"mischievous character\" idea, or if you're just being whimsical for the sake of it.",
      "source": "evaluator"
